* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-vco-period-jitter (issue #518, Part of #16)
* Calibration stage (same circuit as tb_cal_noise.sp.tmpl -- see that
* header), DC-transfer check: sweeps the stage input around the self-bias
* trip point and prints v(sout), so the record can state the small-signal
* gain -dv(sout)/dv(sin1) at the bias point and justify "biased in its
* high-gain linear region" with a number.  Rfb=1e12 stays connected: at
* ~1 V across it the feedback current is ~1 pA, negligible against the
* stage's ~100 uA operating currents, so the driven sweep is not loaded.
*
* Template placeholders: the shared set (see tb_bias_op.sp.tmpl).
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!
.include vco_open.spice
vbiasp vbp 0 dc @VBP@
vbiasn vbn 0 dc @VBN@
vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
vsub sub! 0 dc 0
xs1 sin1 vbp vbn sout vdd 0 vco_stage
rfb sout sin1 1e12
vsin sin1 0 dc @VTRIP@
.control
pre_osdi @OSDI@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/r3_cmc.osdi
dc vsin @VLO@ @VHI@ @VSTEP@
set numdgt=15
print v(sout)
.endc
.end
